<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Monroe is a 30-year-old actor who comes for her yearly preventive visit, nine weeks after her first visit for painful periods. Endometriosis with a left ovarian endometrioma was diagnosed by ultrasound at the gynecology consultation. On the continuous combined pill she has had no periods, only two days of light spotting, and her worst pelvic pain has fallen; she has used naproxen on only a few days. Pain with deep intercourse persists. The bladder infection last month cleared within two days of nitrofurantoin. She has had six sessions of cognitive behavioral therapy, sleeps better, and stopped diphenhydramine. She married this summer. She would like to try for a pregnancy in about a year and wants to know what to do before then. Her PHQ-9 today is 8. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 30</td></tr><tr><td>Endometriosis</td><td>No periods on the continuous pill; less pain; deep pain with intercourse persists</td></tr><tr><td>Pregnancy plans</td><td>Would like to try in about a year</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 8, from 12; item 9 scored 0; six therapy sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Better; diphenhydramine stopped</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on a tablet in the waiting room and reviewed with her by Dr. Whitlock. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, better than in the spring</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Supported by her spouse and a close friend; working again without missed days this month</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>AUDIT-C 2; no drugs; no opioid or sedative use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks 30 to 40 minutes most days; dance and movement classes for work</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; dairy or fortified foods daily</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours most nights, at regular times</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual and reproductive health</td><td>One male partner, her spouse; continuous combined pill; would like a pregnancy in about a year</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe; no one hurts, threatens, or controls her; no firearm in the home</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

