    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Severe painful periods since her teens, worse over the past three years, with pelvic pain between periods, deep pain with intercourse, and painful bowel movements during periods; she misses work for two or three days each cycle. Tender, slightly fixed retroverted uterus with tenderness and fullness in the left adnexa and along the left uterosacral ligament. Suspected endometriosis; transvaginal ultrasound and gynecology consultation booked</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N94.6</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem linked to her documented endometriosis; superseded by the diagnosis at the consultation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Endometriosis: a 3.4 cm left ovarian endometrioma on transvaginal ultrasound, with a tender, thickened left uterosacral ligament and no deep nodule of the bowel or bladder seen; diagnosed from imaging and examination without surgery, as the ESHRE guideline allows. Synthetic modern episode linked to her documented endometriosis</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N80.102</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the gynecology consultation; depth is unspecified because no surgery was done.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate: about two months of low mood, poor sleep on painful nights, low energy, guilt about missed work, and poor concentration (PHQ-9 12, item 9 scored 0; GAD-7 8); Mood Disorder Questionnaire negative; no thoughts of suicide or self-harm</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F32.1</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; the historical and retrospective mental-health accounts are not coded.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Acute uncomplicated cystitis: one day of burning, frequency and urgency with suprapubic discomfort, without fever, flank pain or blood in the urine; urine dipstick positive for leukocyte esterase and nitrite; culture grew Escherichia coli sensitive to nitrofurantoin; resolved</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N30.00</td><td>S — Synthetic acute infection; not a historical claim.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

