    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Pregnancy-intention counseling: she would like to try in about a year, so she continues the continuous pill for pain control until then. Preconception steps started today: folic acid, review of immunity, and a plan to stop the pill at a preconception visit. Her MMR and varicella vaccinations are documented as two doses each, so no immunity tests are needed. [S]<list><item>Folic acid 0.4 mg daily, starting now.</item><item>Preconception visit before she stops the pill.</item><item>Influenza vaccine at the next visit, when the autumn supply is given.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Endometriosis with a left ovarian endometrioma (N80.102)</content>. Pain much improved on continuous suppression; deep pain with intercourse persists and will be assessed with a full pelvic examination at the review next month. No migraine with aura, blood pressure normal, non-smoker: the combined pill remains suitable. [S]<list><item>Continue the continuous combined pill.</item><item>Endometriosis review in four weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 8, from 12: improving with cognitive behavioral therapy and better pain control, but not yet a 50% response. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline are in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue therapy.</item><item>PHQ-9 and GAD-7 at the review in four weeks; discuss an antidepressant if the PHQ-9 has not fallen by half.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>110/70 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 8, from 12 at intake; item 9 scored 0; under treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>GAD-7 8 at intake; repeated at the endometriosis reviews</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 2</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Last cytology four years ago was normal; primary HPV test collected today, every five years if negative</td></tr><tr><td>Contraception and pregnancy intention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Would like a pregnancy in about a year; continuous combined pill continued for endometriosis pain and contraception until then; no condition that rules out estrogen</td></tr><tr><td>Folic acid</td><td>Completed today</td><td>0.4 mg daily started for a woman planning a pregnancy</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; she feels safe</td></tr><tr><td>Chlamydia and gonorrhea screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Negative at the first visit as part of the pelvic pain evaluation; one partner</td></tr><tr><td>HIV and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No result on record; once-in-a-lifetime tests drawn today with her agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 30 with a BMI of 20.5 and no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>To be given at the next visit, when the autumn supply arrives</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed; she will decide at the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap five years ago; Tdap again in each pregnancy</td></tr><tr><td>Measles, mumps, rubella and varicella</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two documented doses of each; immune before pregnancy</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Series completed in adolescence</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Guideline basis: U.S. Medical Eligibility Criteria for Contraceptive Use, 2024 (2024); U.S. Selected Practice Recommendations for Contraceptive Use, 2024 (2024); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HPV, HIV, and hepatitis C results by phone. Endometriosis review in four weeks with a pelvic examination, PHQ-9, GAD-7, and the influenza vaccine. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1956-09-14: three-month review on continuous hormonal treatment: pain, bleeding, mood, and pain with intercourse. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

